{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790923990,"nonce":"HlFVTff7n3zbSNe1IpU1wy1jWYo=","message":"**Governing comment (2026-10-02, after ADR 0055). This supersedes the body and comment #1. Read nothing above this as live.**\n\n**What is left to build: the echo, and only the echo.** When a webhook delivery of an Incident fact gets a 2xx response, oto records the external incident's `external_url` and/or `external_id` once per (Incident, channel) as the outbound mapping of ADR 0052 §5, and shows the link on the Incident's Slack card and page. A response without them is not an error. This is the receipt of a delivery, like a Slack `ts`, not the incident's state; nothing else is read back.\n\n*Where the values come from.*\n1. **By default** — a Connection with no payload mapping — oto reads the top-level keys `external_url` and `external_id` from a 2xx JSON response body. This part is unblocked and can ship first.\n2. **When the Connection carries a payload mapping** (ADR 0055 §2), the mapping's response path wins: oto reads only where the mapping's path points, and does not also look for the default keys. That extraction is built by 2205620; this ticket consumes what it returns. **Only this part is blocked by 2205620.**\n\n*Constraints, because this reads receiver bytes.* `internal/channels/providers/webhook/channel.go:142-145` drains and discards the response, and `recordResponse` (`channel.go:283-298`) says \"IT MUST NEVER CARRY ONE BYTE THE RECEIVER SENT\" because a body snippet made every webhook an SSRF read primitive. That rule still governs `provider_response`, which does not change. The two echoed values are the only bytes kept: parsed from the existing `maxResponseBytes`-bounded read, only on a 2xx, `external_url` only if it is an absolute `https` URL under a stated length, `external_id` only if printable and under a stated length; anything else is treated as absent, never as a failure. The same validation applies to values a mapping's path returns. `domain.DeliverResult` (`internal/channels/domain/ports.go:250-254`) needs a field to carry them; whichever of this ticket and 2205620 lands first adds it.\n\n*Recording.* Once per (Incident, channel): the first valid echo is kept and a retry or a later fact does not overwrite it, so a retried delivery is idempotent.\n\n**What moved out of this ticket.** Comment #1's item 2 (the written contract: `incident.id` as the de-duplication key, the five facts and their meanings, `quiet` is never a resolve) is now 2765f74 (`docs/setup/webhook.md`) and 6ba1847 (`docs/setup/incident-tools.md`). Its item 3 (recipes for two tools) is now 2b5eecc's two starter mappings in the catalog. Do neither here.\n\n⚠️ **Expect the echo to be empty for the two vendors 2b5eecc starts with.** PagerDuty Events v2 answers `202` with `status`, `message`, `dedup_key` (https://docs.pagerduty.com/developer/api/reference/events-v2/send-event/create-v2-event), and incident.io's HTTP alert endpoint answers `202` with `deduplication_key`, `message`, `status` (https://docs.incident.io/openapi/tags/alert-events-v2.json). Neither returns an external incident URL or id; both alert endpoints open incidents asynchronously. The echo is populated by a bridge (ADR 0055 §3) or a receiver that returns the keys. That is not a reason to skip it: test it against a stub receiver.\n\n**Done when.** A stub receiver answering 2xx with `{\"external_url\":\"https://…\",\"external_id\":\"…\"}` gets the link on the Incident's card and page; a retry of the same delivery records nothing new; a receiver answering with no keys, non-JSON, a non-https URL or an oversized value behaves exactly as today with the delivery `sent`; `provider_response` still carries no receiver byte; once 2205620 has landed, a Connection whose mapping names a response path is read only at that path and its default keys are ignored; a test asserts no envelope oto's own code sends carries a resolve, close or status command (the catalog's equivalent check is 2b5eecc's).\n\n**Blocked by.** None for the default echo; 2205620 for the mapping-path part only.\n\n**Mode.** AFK.","files":null}]}